/-!
# Chapter 10 exceptional consumer

The binary source exports now construct the raw G₂(2)′ parabolic
equivalence on the full original endpoints and Borel. The small-unitary
enlargement applications exclude both SU₃(2) and PSU₃(2), including the
actual order-144 projective enlargement. The exhaustive beta selection,
saturated elementary core section and field-power relation are re-exported.
The field-four source now constructs the quintic actor, proves the rank
bound, and recognizes the actual beta core as the minus extraspecial model.
The original alpha core is special of order sixty-four. The source Cartan
centralizes its center, and elementary alpha subgroups meet the beta core
precisely in their alpha-center part. Two actual neighboring-core intersections
are now anisotropic sixteen-groups with distinct square values; they intersect
in the alpha center and generate its core. The alpha cubic balances the three
nonidentity central square fibers. The factor centralizer is now the alpha
center, yielding an actual UT₃(F₄) identification of the alpha core. Its two
elementary planes provide two distinct original Cartan-invariant four-groups,
each disjoint from the beta core and supplementing it to the full Borel
two-core. Gaschütz now splits the beta enlargement modulo its center.
The constructed central preimage has order 120, contains that same Cartan,
and has the literal order-eight intersection with the Borel two-core as
its Sylow two-subgroup. Both invariant four-groups and the original quotient
map are retained together. The anisotropic intersection now exhausts the
beta involution's nontrivial square fiber in the alpha core. Its intersection
with the central preimage supplies an involution outside the kernel, so the
central A₅ double-cover theorem splits that preimage. Its derived subgroup
gives an actual order-sixty complement to the beta enlargement's two-core,
containing the same Cartan and marked by the literal PSL₂(4) quotient map.
The faithful complement action now gives an explicit semidirect-product
realization with the actual core and complement coordinates. The complete
conjugation image is identified with the native J₂ first endpoint's image,
constructing the central-quotient comparison with the original core inclusion
square and representative action equation. The vanishing five-point cocycle
now conjugates the actual complement actions. A native A₅ complement lifts
the comparison to an isomorphism of the entire order-1920 beta enlargement,
with the exact core square and original PSL₂(4) quotient marking. Sylow
conjugacy aligns its order-384 Borel intersection with the native Borel and
gives both inclusion squares. The five-point action and reduced Sylow order
now prove that this enlargement is the full reduced beta endpoint and its
Borel intersection is the entire reduced Borel. Their maps preserve both
inclusion squares and the original PSL₂(4) quotient representatives. The
original extension application constructs the A₅/S₅ beta quotient alternatives
and the common index one or two for both endpoints, the full Borel and S.
The common Sylow comparison now carries the original alpha core to the native
J₂ second core, and preserves its action by the whole reduced Borel. The full
alpha endpoint has order 1152 and quotient S₃ × C₃, retaining the literal
original alpha actor quotient. Its central cubic coset is constructed, and
the common original index gives alpha endpoint and quotient orders 1152n and
18n alongside the beta/Borel/Sylow orders. The compatible full alpha endpoint
isomorphism, remaining original endpoint maps, and Chapter 10 path and
residual conclusions still require their source arguments.

This is the literal 10.9 consumer for the Hall--Janko alternative.  The raw
parabolic equivalence remains an input from the Chapter 10 recognition proof;
the theorem combines it with the saturated-seed parameter calculation and
retains the original endpoint, whole Borel and order-32 core facts.  No
ambient completion isomorphism is inferred from `ParabolicEquiv`.

The terminal-residual extension also exports (10.8) for all characteristic-two
linear markings, the exact strict residual order |R_alpha| = q_beta, and the
strict path parameters in every field, including binary alpha. The exact
strict endpoint-core, D-subgroup and full Borel two-core orders are also
exported, together with the beta Frattini and derived-subgroup identities.
The same opposite-center conjugator and original core maps are retained
through separation, the order calculation and the seven-path argument.
The same marked universal cover transfers the unrestricted strict profile
to the original Chapter 14 tree, with seven-path transitivity and odd fixers.

The strict residual generates the alpha center by core commutators and the
beta core by beta-local conjugation. For every nonbinary beta field, including
binary alpha, the original beta enlargement satisfies [Q_beta,L_beta] = Q_beta
and O²(L_beta) = L_beta. The full beta-stabilizer action on Q_beta/Z_beta
is now irreducible for every nonbinary beta field.

The p.165 minimal-normal-section choice is also exported at the original
reduced boundary: whenever the source strict inclusion Z_beta < Q_beta is
available, the chosen N/Z_beta is a literal minimal normal section of the
finite beta stabilizer, with its quotient action and irreducibility retained.
The strict original source application now supplies Z_beta < Q_beta itself
and chooses a minimal interval under the full original beta stabilizer.
For a proper numerator it proves |Q_beta/N| >= q_beta² and
|N/Z_beta| <= q_alpha². A section smaller than q_beta² lies in Z(L_beta).
The source center argument now excludes that small central section: Cartan
root generation would make D_alpha central in Q_alpha, contradicting the
strict residual commutator. Thus every nonzero beta-invariant section has
order at least q_beta squared. Every proper nonzero invariant section forces
equal fields and has both order and index q_beta squared. For unequal fields,
the original quotient action is irreducible, including the strict mixed
binary/field-four section of order 64 under the full original beta quotient.
For a proper equal-field section, its intersections with Z_alpha and D_alpha
are now exactly Z_beta, and its intersection with Q_alpha has order q_beta
squared. The same section escapes Q_alpha. Its abelian supplement forces the
two-core of the full radius-two kernel strictly between Z_beta and Q_beta,
contradicting that escape. The original quotient action is therefore
irreducible also for equal fields. The complete marked strict profile below
combines this with the binary quaternion alternative, r=6, s=7, odd fixers,
and the exact D and Borel two-core orders.

Source: DGS, *Groups and Graphs* (1985), (10.8)--(10.10), pp.159--165.
-/

